
On windows, the cmake generated folder operates with Visual studio tools viz., msbuild.

I want to stay away from that and stick with cmake.

# Build
cmake --build . --target ALL_BUILD --config Release -v

# Build specific_target.vcproj. Drop the .vcproj when specifying target
cmake --build . --target specific_target --config Release -v

# To run all Unit Tests (yes this is nasty and slow)
cmake --build . --target RUN_TESTS --config Release -v

<edit>
ctest -j 10 # much better Unixy way to go 

# Clean 
cmake --build . --target clean --config Release -v

# parallel Jobs
Append --parallel 20 to cmake commands to speed up using jobs

